abstract: >-
  Unpublished candidate metadata for the code, pre-declarations, provenance
  manifests, and evaluation artifacts accompanying a narrow modular study of a
  gradient-active left-causal depthwise FIR residual in an HSTU-style sequential
  recommender. The fail-closed graph recomputes 198 active paper cells across 22
  families and preserves null, deviated, and VOID outcomes. An equal-parameter
  current-position-only placebo discriminates learned FIR from that tested compound
  placebo in an outcome-known setting but does not isolate temporal access. A
  prospectively frozen MovieLens 1M study did not replicate learned FIR versus identity
  or pointwise; smaller FIR arms met a noninferiority margin only conditionally on that
  failed effect gate. The evidence does not support broad SOTA,
  paired superiority over single-run comparators, per-channel-tap necessity,
  independent confirmation, or generalization. Replace the author placeholder
  and verify legal/licensing fields before publication.
